<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila Central Bank drops special T-bill rates.</title>
<headline>Manila Central Bank drops special T-bill rates.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank said on Tuesday it lowered its borrowing rate on special series Treasury bills.</p>
<p>Its 86-day bill now fetches a rate of 10.70 from 10.85 percent; and its 177-day bill, 11.00 from 11.15 percent.</p>
<p>Traders said the adjustments by the Central Bank were made to align it with the current T-bill rates.</p>
<p>On Monday, the benchmark 91-day Treasury bill rate fell to an average of 10.746 from from 11.172 percent.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
